{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfaeZzBraHt7ps4YRcdwk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is wired into the right units — the format logic stays in `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, and `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` correctly needs only a doc update since it builds off the already-assigned `customerCode` string. The OpenAI spec/examples are kept in sync. One structural issue:\n\n- **Duplicated \"first three letters, upper-cased\" idiom** in `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.service`:\n  ```java\n  String city3 = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length())).toUpperCase();\n  ...\n  String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();\n  ```\n  These two lines are the same transformation applied to two fields. The spec itself defines CITY3 and LAST3 with identical derivation rules, so the shared concept (\"upper-cased first three letters\") deserves a single named unit. Extract a small private helper, e.g.:\n  ```java\n  private static String first3Upper(String s) {\n      return s.substring(0, Math.min(3, s.length())).toUpperCase();\n  }\n  ```\n  and call `first3Upper(city)` / `first3Upper(lastName)`. This removes the duplication, names the intent, and keeps the two segments guaranteed-consistent if the rule ever changes (length, locale on `toUpperCase`, etc.).\n\nNothing else about altitude or placement is off — the per-city sequence filter correctly lives alongside the code assembly, and no class is turning into a catch-all."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10341,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10341},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool